```http
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ0b2tlbl90eXBlIjoiYWNjZXNzIiwiZXhwIjoxNzkxOTgyNTI0LCJpYXQiOjE3OTE5NTM3MjQsImp0aSI6ImYyNGZmYjczOGQ4NzRlZGQ5MzQ4NjY3ZTE2NmYwZmFkIiwidXNlcl9pZCI6MiwiaXNfc3VwZXJhZG1pbiI6ZmFsc2UsImlzX2hyX2FkbWluIjp0cnVlLCJpc19lbXBsb3llZSI6ZmFsc2UsImlzX2hyIjpmYWxzZX0.JNSuz-Mhd-Qr6Fo2c1AxvoxXRH-TGvugmDF7-m0YE5E
@debitNoteId = 3
@vendorId = 1
@billId = 1

### 1. Get Debit Note KPI Card Metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/kpi/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2. List Debit Notes (Paginated with Filters & Search)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/?status=open&search=Chicking
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 3. Filter Debit Notes by Vendor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/?vendor={{vendorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 4. Get Bill Details for Debit Note Construction
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/bill-details/?bill={{billId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 5. Create Debit Note as Draft
# The draft should not create a journal entry.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vendor": {{vendorId}},
  "bill": {{billId}},
  "issue_date": "2026-10-13",
  "reason": "damaged_goods",
  "status": "draft",
  "notes": "Damaged goods returned to vendor",
  "discount": "0.00",
  "items": [
    {
      "bill_item": 1,
      "product": 1,
      "item_name": "Product 1 description",
      "billed_qty": "400.00",
      "already_debited_qty": "0.00",
      "quantity": "80.00",
      "rate": "18.50",
      "vat_percentage": "15.00"
    }
  ]
}

###

### 6. Get Debit Note Detail by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/{{debitNoteId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 7. Issue Debit Note (Draft -> Open)
# Expected: journal entry created automatically.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/{{debitNoteId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "open"
}

###

### 8. Verify Debit Note Journal Entry
# Replace the source_id with the actual debit note ID.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/journal-entries/?source_module=debit_note&source_id={{debitNoteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 9. Update Debit Note Applied Amount
# Use an amount within the debit note's outstanding balance.
# The status should update to partially_applied or closed.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/{{debitNoteId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applied_amount": "500.00"
}

###

### 10. Update Debit Note Notes
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/{{debitNoteId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Updated debit note remarks"
}

###

### 11. Export Debit Notes CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/export/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. Delete Debit Note
# Allowed only if no journal entry has been posted.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/finance/debit-notes/{{debitNoteId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
```